{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":491859,"name":"Jonathan","username":"Johnsters","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/johnsters/{size}/14750_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-15T13:48:19.971Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi All,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am a little confused on what exactly the purpose is of Grok Bot. I see that it’s somehow pushed via Cursor and I went and downloaded Grok Bot to check it out. But can someone explain to me what exactly Grok Bot is and what it’s meant to accomplish?\u003cbr\u003e\nIs Cursor and Grok Bot supposed to work hand in hand and why would I use Grok Bot instead of just Cursor? I got a prompt from Cursor telling me that my prompt can be done in Grok Bot, but why? Is it better at it? What exactly can Grok Bot do that cursor cannot?  What is the benefit of using Grok Bot instead of cursor. I feel like I am missing something here, I want to use the best tool for the job and it feels like Cursor in itself is leaning more towards using Grok Bot then Cursor IDE itself.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs Grok Bot special in some other way?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAny help would be greatly appreciated.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T13:54:13.531Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":138,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":693.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171745,"topic_slug":"confused-over-grok-bot","display_username":"Jonathan","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":4,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":15670,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/confused-over-grok-bot/171745/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":491873,"name":"Jonathan","username":"Johnsters","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/johnsters/{size}/14750_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-15T14:09:46.162Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI used Grok Bot to explain, and this is what it says, I think I understand a little better now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot is a standing assistant you chat with outside the editor. Cursor IDE is where you write and change code in a project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePurpose of Grok Bot.\u003c/strong\u003e It’s a desktop companion that can help across your day: engineering work (including spinning up Cursor cloud agents on repos), local files on a connected machine, schedules and “watch this for me” routines, connectors (Slack, GitHub, and so on), and browser/desktop tasks on its own computer. You create agents with roles (like this \u003ca href=\"http://ASP.NET\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eASP.NET\u003c/a\u003e one), and they keep going even when you’re not in a coding session.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow that differs from Cursor IDE.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor IDE is the coding environment: open a workspace, edit files, use inline/chat agents that live inside that project context.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot is the chat app beside that: multi-agent sidebar, longer-running help, routines while you’re away, and tools that reach beyond one open folder (your registered computers, cloud agents, messaging, bookings, etc.).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepo changes from here usually go through a Cursor cloud agent (branch/PR), not by silently rewriting files in your IDE buffer. Local file work on your PC needs your approval per action.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor IDE chat history does not automatically carry over here (as you saw with your current workspace). You bring context by pointing at a repo, path, PR, or pasting a recap.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn practice: use Cursor when you’re deep in the code; use me when you want an always-on helper that can coordinate that work, watch things, or handle the non-editor side.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T14:09:46.162Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":18.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171745,"topic_slug":"confused-over-grok-bot","display_username":"Jonathan","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://ASP.NET","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"ASP.NET Core, an open-source web development framework | .NET","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":15670,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/confused-over-grok-bot/171745/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":493473,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T05:26:14.329Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, good request. Let’s break it down step by step.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor and Grok Bot are two different products that share one account and one subscription:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor is for development. The agent works inside your code, in the editor, in cloud agents, and in the CLI.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot is an AI teammate for everything outside the editor. It runs on its own always-on cloud computer with a browser, files, and a terminal, connects to your tools (email, calendar, docs, etc.), and finishes tasks there. You can set up routines that run on a schedule, and keep chatting from your phone.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe message you saw in Cursor is just a tip. It shows up when the first message in a new chat looks like a non-coding task (writing an email, doing research, putting together a doc). Cursor will still answer that request. It’s only saying Grok Bot is designed for those tasks. It doesn’t mean Grok Bot is better at coding. For anything related to your codebase, the right tool is Cursor. And when Grok Bot needs to write code, it still hands that off to the Cursor cloud agent in your account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you don’t want the tip, close it with the X. It only shows on the first message of a new chat and only a limited number of times, so it will stop showing up on its own over time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbout quota: on Pro, Grok Bot has a separate weekly allowance, so trying it won’t use your Cursor quota. More details are in the nearby thread: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/does-grok-bot-consume-cursor-quota/171742\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eDoes Grok bot consume cursor quota?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA more complete overview is here: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/introducing-grok-bot/168053\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eIntroducing Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour explanation in the post above is basically correct. You’ve already got the main idea. Let me know if you still have questions.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T05:26:14.329Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":12,"readers_count":11,"score":7.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171745,"topic_slug":"confused-over-grok-bot","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/does-grok-bot-consume-cursor-quota/171742","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Does Grok bot consume cursor quota?","clicks":4},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/introducing-grok-bot/168053","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Introducing Grok Bot","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/confused-over-grok-bot/171745/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":493553,"name":"Jonathan","username":"Johnsters","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/johnsters/{size}/14750_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:01:07.920Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks Dean, I understand much better now.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T07:01:07.920Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incom